# PX4 parameters for AeroPACT fleet vehicles in SITL, applied on every boot (PX4_PARAM_*).
# Format: NAME VALUE  # why. Hardware vehicles take the same set through a QGroundControl
# parameter file; the site-specific lines are marked SITE and must be reviewed per deployment.

# Command and control: the companion computer flies the vehicle; there is no RC transmitter
# and no ground station in SITL. SITE: on hardware keep an RC link for the safety pilot (mode 0)
# and choose the data-link-loss action with the operator.
COM_RC_IN_MODE 4
NAV_DLL_ACT 0
# Companion computer lost (offboard stream silent for 1 s): the autopilot returns home on its own.
COM_OF_LOSS_T 1.0
COM_OBL_RC_ACT 3
# Return-to-launch: climb above the tallest buildings before returning. The launcher adds a
# per-vehicle offset so simultaneous returns are vertically separated. SITE: survey heights.
RTL_RETURN_ALT 60
RTL_DESCEND_ALT 20
# Envelope matching the fleet stack's limits (safety_policy.yaml).
MPC_XY_VEL_MAX 12.0
MPC_Z_VEL_MAX_UP 3.0
MPC_Z_VEL_MAX_DN 3.0
# Flight termination may be commanded (fault injection: kill_drone). SITE: decide with the
# operator whether a companion computer may terminate; a parachute changes the answer.
CBRK_FLIGHTTERM 0
# The pack is modelled by the AeroPACT vehicle plant (payload, charging pads, drain faults);
# PX4's simulated battery stays above its failsafe thresholds so it never acts on a fake pack.
SIM_BAT_MIN_PCT 50
# Realistic simulated discharge (full pack in ~30 min instead of PX4's 60 s default). Where the
# autopilot's battery is the source of truth (vehicle.launch.py, the distributed rehearsal) the
# safety supervisor's endurance check measures this rate; at the default it grounds the vehicle
# seconds after take-off.
SIM_BAT_DRAIN 1800
